From: LUgABeEEE <LUgABeEEE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:06:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(android): reuse revalidated boot batches with
 ownership-safe cancellation

Restores #314's device-side boot-batch cache, which upstream deferred in 0.8.1,
and addresses the four conditions named there: request cancellation, durable-body
consistency, clear-versus-download isolation and benefit measurement.

- BootAssetStore: per-entry SHA-256, .part + fsync + atomic rename, epoch and
  per-key version checks on commit, one writer per key, entry bound, and a clear
  that only drops unreferenced entries and aborts in-flight commits.
- HttpBootAssetFetcher: cancellation through disconnect(), Content-Length and
  decoded-body digest checks, bounded 6s intercept budget so WebView can retake
  the request instead of waiting on a stuck read.
- BootAssetCache and BootAssetMetrics: one WebView bridge with a null fallback on
  any failure, plus hit/miss/fetched/saved counters where
  savedPercent = saved / (saved + fetched).
- Wiring in SecureWebViewClient and MainActivity; design, evidence and remaining
  device work in apps/mobile/android/BOOT_CACHE_PATCH.md.
